ok 1 - fixture: producer rows exist in eleven of the twelve tables
ok 2 - only the template binding table lacks a producer row, because no producer can write one [P2-S09-AC-165]
ok 3 - the eleven owned tables carry NOT NULL id, owner_id, version, created_at and updated_at of the envelope types [P2-S09-AC-165]
ok 4 - each of them carries a NOT NULL closed state [P2-S09-AC-165]
ok 5 - the nonce receipt is the one documented exception: no owner, state or version (the release key identifies it) [P2-S09-AC-165]
ok 6 - every version column is closed to non-positive values [P2-S09-AC-165]
ok 7 - every state is a closed enum or a CHECK over a finite list [P2-S09-AC-165]
ok 8 - the six tables whose CAS version advances are guarded against a decrease; the other five are immutable and pin version 1 [P2-S09-AC-165]
ok 9 - artifacts, blocks and lifecycle events never leave version 1 [P2-S09-AC-165]
ok 10 - artifacts, block versions and lifecycle events pin updated_at = created_at in a CHECK [P2-S09-AC-166]
ok 11 - a renewed updated_at on an artifact is rejected by exactly that CHECK [P2-S09-AC-166]
ok 12 - and on a block version [P2-S09-AC-166]
ok 13 - and on a lifecycle event [P2-S09-AC-166]
ok 14 - every stored immutable row has updated_at = created_at [P2-S09-AC-166]
true
ok 15 - an UPDATE of a block version is rejected [P2-S09-AC-166]
ok 16 - a DELETE of a block version is rejected [P2-S09-AC-166]
ok 17 - an UPDATE of a lifecycle event is rejected [P2-S09-AC-166]
ok 18 - a DELETE of a lifecycle event is rejected [P2-S09-AC-166]
ok 19 - a DELETE of an artifact is rejected [P2-S09-AC-166]
true
ok 20 - an artifact whose version has left draft cannot be updated even in the compile context [P2-S09-AC-166]
ok 21 - no function renews updated_at on an immutable table [P2-S09-AC-166]
ok 22 - cms_content_types persists identity, owner, state, version, timestamps, the immutable type key, owner capability, built-in flag and creator [P2-S09-AC-167]
ok 23 - the type key is unique: a duplicate row collides, a distinct key does not, so keys are never reused [P2-S09-AC-167]
ok 24 - the owner/state and owner/time indexes exist [P2-S09-AC-167]
ok 25 - the type key is an immutable identity: a rename is rejected [P2-S09-AC-167]
ok 26 - cms_content_type_versions persists the parent type, version number, workflow and locale references, template and artifact references, definition hash, compatibility, supersession, dry run and the frozen activation evidence [P2-S09-AC-168]
ok 27 - a type has at most one active version: a second active row collides, a superseded copy does not [P2-S09-AC-168]
ok 28 - a successor records its supersession and the activated version holds the server-frozen evidence (policy, decision count, approval hash) [P2-S09-AC-168]
ok 29 - cms_content_type_capability_bindings persists the parent version, the protected capability key and version and the envelope [P2-S09-AC-170]
ok 30 - one binding per (version, key, version) is enforced [P2-S09-AC-170]
ok 31 - cms_field_definition_versions persists the stable identity, key, kind, constraints, validator, default, localization, editor config and lifecycle [P2-S09-AC-171]
ok 32 - the field key is unique within a type version [P2-S09-AC-171]
ok 33 - and so is the stable identity [P2-S09-AC-171]
ok 34 - cms_relation_definitions persists the relation field, target kind, type and projection, cardinality, finite bounds, ordering and unavailable behavior [P2-S09-AC-172]
ok 35 - one relation per field [P2-S09-AC-172]
ok 36 - every stored target resolves in the code allowlist, so a relation never escalates authority [P2-S09-AC-172]
ok 37 - cms_schema_migration_plans persists source and target versions, classification, transform, report, cursor, progress, counters, worker state and timestamps [P2-S09-AC-173]
ok 38 - one live plan per (from, to) version pair: a second live plan collides, a superseded one does not [P2-S09-AC-173]
ok 39 - the migration states are the closed nine-member set [P2-S09-AC-173]
ok 40 - cms_schema_artifacts persists the compiler, contract reference, manifests, hash and composite ownership link [P2-S09-AC-174]
ok 41 - one artifact per type version [P2-S09-AC-174]
ok 42 - the composite ownership FK from version to artifact is deferred [P2-S09-AC-174]
ok 43 - an artifact is terminal: the only state is compiled [P2-S09-AC-174]
ok 44 - the twelve tables carry 20 unique constraints [P2-S09-AC-178]
ok 45 - and 23 foreign keys [P2-S09-AC-178]
ok 46 - and 20 further indexes, owner, time and query indexes and the partial unique ones among them [P2-S09-AC-178]
ok 47 - the owner indexes are present [P2-S09-AC-178]
ok 48 - both partial unique indexes (one active version per type, one live plan per pair) are present [P2-S09-AC-178]
ok 49 - every plain unique constraint of a table with rows rejects a duplicate producer row and accepts a distinct key [P2-S09-AC-178]
ok 50 - every foreign key of a table with rows rejects a dangling value [P2-S09-AC-178]
ok 51 - the template binding unique pair is declared (no producer row exists to probe it) [P2-S09-AC-178]
ok 52 - keys and immutable evidence are never reused or rewritten: the immutable evidence tables reject updates (proved above) and the keys are unique [P2-S09-AC-178]
ok 53 - a mismatched artifact pair is accepted by the statement and refused when the deferred constraint is checked, in the same transaction, before it can commit [P2-S09-AC-179]
ok 54 - the aggregate is created inside one SECURITY DEFINER function, so all its foreign keys are checked at that transaction's commit [P2-S09-AC-179]
ok 55 - a registry or UUID reference that does not resolve (here an unknown template version) is refused before any aggregate row becomes visible [P2-S09-AC-179]
ok 56 - nine of the tables refuse DELETE by a dedicated trigger (six definition tables and the three immutable ones) [P2-S09-AC-185]
ok 57 - no function deletes a definition, a version, a plan or a report: active and superseded definitions and migration evidence are retained [P2-S09-AC-185]
ok 58 - retirement is a state value on the type row, beside active (a never activated type is physically retired): states, not deletions, carry the lifecycle [P2-S09-AC-185]
ok 59 - a migration plan cannot be deleted [P2-S09-AC-185]
ok 60 - no purge, legal-hold or incident-fence object exists for the registry: nothing can purge, and no hold mechanism is modelled [P2-S09-AC-185]
